<title>UZBEKISTAN: Uzbek cotton harvest starts, good crop expected.</title>
<headline>Uzbek cotton harvest starts, good crop expected.</headline>
<dateline>TASHKENT 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uzbek farmers started harvesting raw cotton last week and have gathered 317,000 tonnes so far, a statement issued by the cotton department of the Central Asian state's agriculture ministry said.</p>
<p>The department gave no comparison for the previous year.</p>
<p>The agriculture ministry has said it expects a good 1996 harvest. The target of four million tonnes of raw cotton is the same as in 1995 when output totalled 3.934 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Average yields from this year's planted area of 1.490 million ha should be no less than 26 centners (2,600 kg) per ha.</p>
<p>Last year's average yield from a planted area of 1.493 million ha was 26.4 centners.</p>
<p>--Tashkent Newsroom, +7 3712 361958</p>
</text>
